# The production picker (ProdPicker) opened from the base screen's CHANGE button, loaded from the game's autosave: the colony pod
# founds the first base (key B), its base screen (Return) shows the production at the bottom left. The picker is a grid of five cells
# to a row over the base screen, four of them filled at this stage of the game, a row of buttons at the foot. A click marks a cell
# (a unit's picture is drawn by the game, a facility's by Chiron), the cursor keys move the mark within the cells, Home goes to the first
# and End to the last. Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
# The leaders' portraits in the base screen animate on their own slow clock.
mask 266 625 310 678
mask 702 624 760 680
25 load
48 click 362 734         # the note's Close
55 key b                 # found a base where the colony pod stands
64 key Return            # its base screen
68 state pp_sel 0x6b27b8 12
68 state pp_grid 0x6b2854 32
68 state pp_mode 0x6a8ba8 16
72 click 175 723         # CHANGE
76 move 600 420          # off the button (its bubble comes later), over an empty cell
80 snap open
82 move 380 120          # over the second cell: nothing happens
86 snap hover
88 click 510 120         # a click marks the third cell
92 snap click-third
94 key Right             # the fourth
98 snap key-right
100 key Right            # the last of the row has no cell: the mark stays on the last cell with a tech
104 snap key-right-end
106 key Left
110 snap key-left
112 key Home             # the first
116 snap key-home
118 key End              # the last choice
122 snap key-end
124 key Down             # nothing below it
128 snap key-down
130 key Up               # nothing above it
134 snap key-up
136 key Left             # the keypad's 4 does the same: not sent here
140 click 240 120         # the first cell
144 snap click-first
146 key Escape            # not used by the window
150 snap key-escape
152 close
